{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QuantumObservableUniverse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QuantumObservableUniverse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneBalancedRibbon","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.ZeroMorphisms","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.Kernels","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Types.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":57,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.gaugeGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.gaugeGroup","kind":"def","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L376-L392","doc":"The **quantum gauge group** `G_q = Aut⊗(ω)`: the group of monoidal\nnatural automorphisms of the fibre functor.\n\nThe full definition is `Aut⊗(ω)` — natural isomorphisms `ω ≅ ω`\nthat are compatible with the monoidal structure (tensor products\nand unit).  The type `ω ≅ ω` captures `Aut(ω)`; the monoidal\nconstraint is enforced by `fibreFunctor_monoidal` on `QuantumUniverse`,\nwhich restricts to monoidal natural transformations.\n\nBy Tannaka–Krein duality, `G_q` is a compact group (or algebraic\ngroup over `k`) that can be recovered from `ω`.\n\nRef: [lusztig1993] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-8176-4717-9 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.volumeIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.volumeIso","kind":"def","line":375,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L375-L375","doc":"**Volume constraint** (condition iii), under the **strong (iso)\nreading**: `ε : Λ²V ≅ 𝟙`, which forces `det(g_V) = 1` for all\n`g ∈ Aut⊗(ω)`, restricting the gauge group from `GL(2)` to `SL(2)`.\n\nWas `volumeForm : exteriorSquare ⟶ (𝟙_ C)` plus a separate\n`volumeForm_epi` field.  Both are subsumed: an isomorphism is epi, so\n`volumeForm_epi` is now a theorem\n(`QOU.epi_of_iso_unit`, `CategoricalFoundations.lean`) rather than a\nhypothesis, and the bare-morphism version admitted `volumeForm := 0`.\nBean `qou-n1dj` item 2 — the editorial choice between the epi and iso\nreadings of \"non-degenerate epimorphism\", resolved to iso.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{eq:categorical-volume-constraint}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquare_epi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquare_epi","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L361-L361","doc":"`Λ²V` is a **quotient** of `V ⊗ V`.  No braiding-eigenvalue condition:\non the `q`-exterior square the braiding acts by `-q⁻¹`, not `-1`, so\ndemanding `β ≫ π = -π` would silently impose `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquareProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquareProj","kind":"def","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L357-L357","doc":"The antisymmetrisation `π : V ⊗ V ↠ Λ²V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exteriorSquare","kind":"def","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L355-L355","doc":"The exterior square `Λ²V` as an object of `C`, presented as a quotient\nof `V ⊗ V` by the two fields below.  Previously a free field with no tie\nto `fundamentalObj`; bean `qou-n1dj` item 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fundamentalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fundamentalObj","kind":"def","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L351-L351","doc":"The fundamental object `V` of categorical dimension 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L349-L349","doc":"**Adjoint vanishing** (condition ii): all morphisms `𝟙 → Ad(A)` in\n`C` are equal.  In an `R`-linear category this is equivalent to\n`Hom_C(𝟙, Ad(A)) = 0`, since the zero morphism is always present\nand all others must equal it.\n\nRead with the three fields above, this now says what the paper says:\nthe *reduced* adjoint has no invariants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L341-L341","doc":"`Ad(A)` is not the zero object.  Together with the two fields above this\nis what `adjointObj := 0` fails: the only morphism out of the zero\nobject is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_augmented","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_augmented","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L337-L337","doc":"**`Ad(A)` carries no trivial summand**: it lands in `ker ε`.\n\nThis is what makes condition (ii) a statement with content.  The full\n`A` always contains the unit `η : 𝟙 → A`, so `Hom(𝟙, A) = 0` is false\nfor any nontrivial `A` and cannot be what the axiom means.  The corpus\nis explicit that the trivial part is excluded: `Ad(A)` decomposes \"with\nno spin-0 summand\" (`brings-qou-axiom-map.md`) and is `≅ V₂`, the\n3-dimensional traceless part, for `SU_q(2)` (`brings-is-qou.lean`).\nThat reduced adjoint is taken to land in `ker ε`; this field is part of\nthe data and is not derived from a property of `ε`.  (An earlier\njustification read \"the adjoint action preserves `ker ε` because `ε` is\nan algebra map\".  A multiplicative counit is not available: it forces\n`x = ε(x) • 1` for every `x`, see\n`MultiplicativeCounitCollapse.eq_counit_smul_one`, bean `qou-aj49`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_mono","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L322-L322","doc":"The inclusion is a subobject inclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjointIncl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjointIncl","kind":"def","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L320-L320","doc":"`Ad(A)` sits inside `A`.  The adjoint action is an action of `A` on\nitself, so its carrier is part of `A` rather than an unrelated object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjointObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.adjointObj","kind":"def","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L317-L317","doc":"The adjoint object `Ad(A)` in `C`, carrying the adjoint action of the\nHopf algebra `A` on itself.  In a braided monoidal category it is\nconstructed from `(A, μ, Δ, S)` and the braiding; that construction is\nnot available here, so the object is provided together with the three\nfields below, which pin down enough of its relationship to `A` that a\ndegenerate choice cannot satisfy them.\n\n**This was previously a free field**, with nothing linking it to\n`frobHopf`.  That made `adjoint_vanishing` satisfiable by taking\n`adjointObj := 0` — the zero object has `Hom(𝟙, 0) = 0` trivially — so\nan instance could satisfy \"no hidden global symmetries\" by having no\nadjoint object at all.  See bean `qou-fav8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.rigidInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.rigidInst","kind":"def","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L304-L304","doc":"**Rigidity** (condition 0): every object of `C` has left and right\nduals, with `ev`/`coev` satisfying the snake identities.  A dual is a\nworldline read backwards, so this is the antiparticle condition; it is\nalso what lets a strand bend back on itself and a braid close into a\nknot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.mk","kind":"ctor","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L297-L297","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.toQuantumUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.toQuantumUniverse","kind":"def","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L297-L375","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","kind":"structure","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L281-L375","doc":"**Quantum Observable Universe** over a commutative ring `R`.\n\nA quantum universe that is **rigid** and satisfies three observability\nconditions.  Rigidity (condition 0) is imposed here, not on\n`QuantumUniverse`: a quantum universe is braided, an observable one is\nbraided and rigid.  The remaining conditions:\n(i)   the Frobenius form on `A` is non-degenerate — an exact self-pairing,\n      already enforced structurally by the snake identities in\n      `FrobeniusHopfData`.\n(ii)  `Hom_C(𝟙, Ad(A))` is trivial — no non-trivial invariant adjoint\n      morphisms.\n(iii) categorical volume constraint: the fundamental object `V` of\n      categorical dimension 2 admits a non-degenerate epimorphism\n      `ε : Λ²V → 𝟙` preserved by the rigid dualities.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-observable-universe}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-observable-universe","label":"def:quantum-observable-universe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms_isLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms_isLimit","kind":"def","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L279-L279","doc":"The fork `differentialForms` is a limit: `Ω¹(A)` *is* the kernel of\n`μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.differentialForms","kind":"def","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L276-L276","doc":"**`A` admits a universal first-order calculus.**  `Ω¹(A)` is a\nkernel of the multiplication `μ : A ⊗ A ⟶ A` in `C`: an object with a\nmorphism `ι : Ω¹(A) ⟶ A ⊗ A` such that `ι ≫ μ = 0`, universal among\nsuch.  This is the noncommutative universal calculus, not Mathlib's\n`KaehlerDifferential` (commutative only, and the quotient `I/I²` of\nthis kernel).  In `ModuleCat R` it is realised by\n`QOU.MathlibExt.UniversalDifferentials.Ω1`.  Carried as a fork plus\nits universal property rather than a `HasKernels C` instance: the\npaper needs this one kernel, not every kernel in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L266-L266","doc":"Every block's quantum dimension is a **unit**: each can be normalised\nagainst.  `IsUnit` for the same reason as `frobWeight_isUnit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.dimQ","kind":"def","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L263-L263","doc":"The quantum dimension `dim_q(λ)` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L261-L261","doc":"Every block's Frobenius weight is a **unit**: none is invisible to the\ntrace.  `IsUnit`, not `≠ 0` — the paper says \"invertible in `R`\", and\nover a ring those differ (`2 ≠ 0` in `ℤ`, and `2` is not a unit).  The\ntwo coincide only over a field, which is why `≠ 0` survived while the\nbase ring was one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobWeight","kind":"def","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L255-L255","doc":"The Frobenius weight `∫_A p_λ` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_complete","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L253-L253","doc":"**The blocks span.**  `Σ_λ p_λ = 𝟙_A`: every state resolves into the\nchannels, with nothing left over.  Together with orthogonality this is\nwhat \"Wedderburn decomposition\" means; without it the blocks could sit\ninside `A` without exhausting it.\n\nThis is the field the axiom's NAME promised and its TYPE did not\ndeliver.  It needs the finite sum that `Preadditive` supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L245-L245","doc":"**Blocks do not mix.**  Distinct central idempotents are orthogonal, so a\nstate resolving into one channel has no component in another.  This is the\nhalf of semisimplicity that costs only a zero morphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem_idem","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L241-L241","doc":"Each `p_λ` is idempotent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.centralIdem","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L239-L239","doc":"The central idempotent `p_λ` of each block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocksFintype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocksFintype","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L237-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.blocks","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L236-L236","doc":"**Wedderburn semisimplicity** (axiom 4).  The substrate has *channels*:\n`A` decomposes into finitely many blocks that do not mix, and no block\nis degenerate.\n\nEncoded here: a `Fintype` of blocks, an idempotent endomorphism of `A`\nper block, their mutual orthogonality, their completeness, and\ninvertibility of each block's Frobenius weight and quantum dimension.\n\n**`blocks` indexes the NON-NEGLIGIBLE blocks, and vanishing elsewhere is\npermitted.**  `dimQ_isUnit` below is therefore a specification of what\n`blocks` ranges over, NOT a prohibition on the ambient category.  This\nmatters at a root of unity (and in char p), where some `dim_q(λ)` really\ndoes vanish: those λ are *negligible* — they form a tensor ideal, the\ncategorical trace kills anything factoring through them, and the standard\nconstruction quotients by that ideal (semisimplification) before reading\noff blocks.  Read as a prohibition, the field would exclude the\nroot-of-unity categories outright; read as an index specification, it\nsays the decomposition is that of the semisimplified quotient.\n\nThe corpus already relies on this shape elsewhere: `y_(1^3) ≡ 0` in\n`h3-markov-wenzl-weights` (the Temperley-Lieb quotient kills the 3-row\npartition), and `tr_M = Σ_λ y_λ χ^λ` sums over all λ with zero weights on\nsome.  That vanishing is a DIFFERENT mechanism from negligibility — a row\ncap at generic q, not a root-of-unity phenomenon — but it is the same\npattern, and it is why no sum over blocks needs re-indexing here.\n\nOrthogonality needs a zero morphism and completeness needs a finite\nsum; both come from the `Preadditive` instance field above.\n\n`frobWeight` and `dimQ` land in `R` via `unitEndEquiv`, which is\ncarried as a field rather than left to a docstring — see its comment\nfor why `R`-linearity alone does not supply it (bean `qou-w1g8`).\n\nGiven this axiom, the co-Casimir trace identity\n`tr_M(C_dimQ) = Σ_λ 1/dim_q(λ)` is a *consequence*, proved as\n`QOU.BraidKnot.frobenius_codim_universal` by linearity of the trace\nover the central idempotents.  It is deliberately NOT an axiom here:\nasserting it would assert something already proved, and would collide\nwith the unrelated `def:mass-identity` (the vortex integral). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.unitEndEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.unitEndEquiv","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L196-L196","doc":"**The ground ring is `End(𝟙_C)`.**  The block data below lands in `R`\nrather than in `End(𝟙_C)`, which presumes the two agree.  That is a\ngenuine extra assumption, NOT a consequence of `R`-linearity:\n`Linear R C` supplies only a ring map `R → End(𝟙_C)`, `r ↦ r • 𝟙`,\nand its being bijective needs `𝟙` simple.  Carried explicitly so the\nassumption is visible instead of hiding in a docstring.\n\nSurfaced on the paper side in `def:quantum-universe`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobenius_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobenius_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L186-L186","doc":"**Symmetric Frobenius** (axiom 3).  A closed loop has one amplitude:\nclosing a worldline on the left and closing it on the right compute the\nsame endomorphism of the unit.  Equivalently, the Frobenius form `∫_A`\nis symmetric and the Nakayama automorphism is trivial.\n\nThis is a genuine restriction, not a consequence of axiom 2: a Frobenius\nalgebra whose form is non-symmetric has `leftTrace ≠ rightTrace`, and\nthen \"the trace of a process\" — hence any mass read off a trace — would\ndepend on a drawing convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.fibreFunctor","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L176-L176","doc":"The fibre functor `τ : C → Type*` (abstracting `Vect_R` / `R-Mod`).\nThe paper asks for it to be exact, faithful, `R`-linear and monoidal;\nNONE of those four is carried by this type, which is a bare functor to\n`Type`.  Recorded rather than silently implied — the gap is real and\nseparate from the `R`-linearity of `C` now carried above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.frobHopf","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L170-L170","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.balancedInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.balancedInst","kind":"def","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L168-L168","doc":"**The balancing twist** `θ_X : X ⟶ X` (axiom 1, categorical half).\n\nThis is what makes the substrate parameter `q` *derivable rather than\ncarried*.  On the defining representation the twist axiom forces\n`θ_V = q^{1/2} · id_V` (`rem:sqrt-q-ribbon-structure`), so `q` is read\noff the structure; there is deliberately **no `q` field**, since a\ndistinguished element would smuggle in as data the thing the framework\nclaims to derive.\n\nThree further things it supplies, none of which the previous\n`[BraidedCategory]` alone gave:\n\n1. **Framing.**  Without a twist a braid closure is only a *framed* link\n   invariant — `tr_M(β)` depends on the writhe of the braid word rather\n   than on the knot.  Since masses are read off knots, that dependence\n   would be fatal.\n2. **Sphericality on all of `C`.**  Axiom 3 gives left-trace =\n   right-trace on `End(A)` only, but the Markov trace closes strands of\n   `V^{⊗n}`, not of `A`.  Ribbon = braided + spherical extends it to the\n   objects the knot theory actually uses.\n3. **A legible classical boundary.**  `BalancedCategory.ofSymmetric`\n   proves every symmetric category is balanced with `θ = 𝟙`, so the\n   classical case is `θ = 𝟙`, i.e. `q = 1` — a *describable member*, not\n   an excluded one.  This is why the fix is \"add the twist\", not \"forbid\n   symmetric\": `q → 1` must stay inside the category it is a limit of.\n\nUses the in-repo `BalancedCategory` (bean `rtrb`, sorry-free) since\nMathlib has no ribbon layer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.braidedInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.braidedInst","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L139-L139","doc":"**Temporal braiding.**  The exchange of two adjacent systems is a\nprocess with a direction: `c_{V,W} : V ⊗ W ≅ W ⊗ V`, not required to\nbe symmetric.  Rigidity is deliberately NOT here — it belongs to\n`QuantumObservableUniverse` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.linInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.linInst","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L134-L134","doc":"**`C` is `R`-linear.**  Every hom-set is an `R`-module and composition\nis `R`-bilinear — verbatim `def:rigid-monoidal-category`, and what\n`def:quantum-universe` means by \"an `R`-linear braided monoidal\ncategory\".\n\nThis is `CategoryTheory.Linear`, which takes `Preadditive` as a\nprerequisite; the two are a stack, not alternatives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.preInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.preInst","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L126-L126","doc":"**Hom-sets are abelian groups.**  Carried because the paper's\n`R`-linearity (below) presupposes it, and because two axiom-4 fields\nneed it: the zero morphism for block orthogonality, and a finite sum\nfor block completeness.\n\nNote this REPLACES a bare `HasZeroMorphisms` field.  `Preadditive`\nsupplies zero morphisms already, so carrying both would put two\n`HasZeroMorphisms` instances on `C` and make `p_b ≫ p_b' = 0`\nambiguous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.monInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.monInst","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.catInst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.catInst","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L115-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.C","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L114-L114","doc":"The monoidal category `C`. Represented as an opaque type with\n`Category` and `MonoidalCategory` instances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse.mk","kind":"ctor","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumUniverse","kind":"structure","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L104-L279","doc":"**Quantum Universe** over a commutative ring `R`.\n\nRe-declared from the library module\n`QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations` (see the note\non `FrobeniusHopfData` above).  Keep field-for-field in sync.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-universe}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-universe","label":"def:quantum-universe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/quantum-universe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.rightTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.rightTrace","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L97-L100","doc":"**Right categorical trace** of `f : A → A`, closing the loop on the right:\n`𝟙 →[coev] A ⊗ A →[A ◁ f] A ⊗ A →[ev] 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.leftTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.leftTrace","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L92-L95","doc":"**Left categorical trace** of `f : A → A`, obtained by closing the loop on\nthe left: `𝟙 →[coev] A ⊗ A →[f ▷ A] A ⊗ A →[ev] 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ev","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L88-L90","doc":"**Evaluation** `ev = μ ≫ ∫_A : A ⊗ A → 𝟙`.  Together with `coevaluation`\nand the two snake identities, this exhibits `A` as self-dual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobenius_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobenius_relation","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L80-L80","doc":"**Frobenius relation**: `μ ≫ Δ = (Δ ▷ A) ≫ α ≫ (A ◁ μ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_right","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L76-L76","doc":"**Snake identity (right).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.pairing_snake_left","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L72-L72","doc":"**Snake identity (left).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.coevaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.coevaluation","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Coevaluation morphism `η̃ : 𝟙 → A ⊗ A`, the dual datum to the\nevaluation `ev = μ ≫ λ : A ⊗ A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusForm","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Frobenius form `λ : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.antipode","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Antipode morphism `S : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Counit morphism `ε : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Comultiplication morphism `Δ : A → A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unit","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Unit morphism `η : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mul","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Multiplication morphism `μ : A ⊗ A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.obj","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The underlying object in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData","kind":"structure","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe.lean#L41-L81","doc":"**Frobenius–Hopf data** in a monoidal category.\n\nRe-declared from the library module\n`QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations` so this sibling\nis a self-contained compilation unit — importing the library module\nwould collide with this block's own `QuantumObservableUniverse` and\n`QuantumUniverse.gaugeGroup` declarations.  Keep field-for-field in\nsync with the library.\n\nLaTeX: used in `\\label{def:quantum-universe}`, item (ii).\nRef: [kock2004] ","signatureChunk":0}]}